sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant APIServer as API Server (managed)<br/>8000/TCP HTTP/HTTPS
    participant DB as PostgreSQL / Redis<br/>5432 or 6379/TCP
    participant S3 as S3 / MinIO<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Processor as Processor (managed)<br/>AIMD Concurrency
    participant InfGW as Inference Gateway<br/>HTTP/HTTPS
    participant Redis as Redis MQ<br/>6379/TCP
    participant AsyncProc as Async-Processor (managed)
    participant EPP as Inference Gateway EPP
    participant Prom as Prometheus<br/>9090/TCP

    rect rgb(230, 245, 255)
        Note over Client,S3: Flow 1: Batch Job Submission (Sync Mode)
        Client->>APIServer: POST batch job<br/>Optional TLS, API key, tenant header
        APIServer->>DB: Store job state<br/>Optional TLS, credentials from Secret
        APIServer->>S3: Store input files<br/>TLS, S3 credentials from Secret
        APIServer-->>Client: Job ID response

        Processor->>DB: Poll pending jobs<br/>Optional TLS, credentials from Secret
        Processor->>InfGW: Dispatch inference requests<br/>Optional TLS/mTLS, API key
        InfGW-->>Processor: Inference results
        Processor->>S3: Store output files<br/>TLS, S3 credentials
        Processor->>DB: Update job status
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 230)
        Note over Client,Prom: Flow 2: Batch Job Submission (Async Mode)
        Client->>APIServer: POST batch job<br/>Optional TLS, API key, tenant header
        APIServer->>DB: Store job state
        APIServer-->>Client: Job ID response

        Processor->>Redis: Enqueue inference tasks<br/>Optional TLS, credentials from Secret
        AsyncProc->>Redis: Dequeue tasks (sorted-set poll)<br/>Optional TLS, credentials from Secret
        AsyncProc->>Prom: Query gate metrics (optional)<br/>HTTP, no auth
        AsyncProc->>EPP: Dispatch to EndpointPicker<br/>Optional TLS/mTLS, API key
        EPP-->>AsyncProc: Inference results
    end

    rect rgb(230, 255, 230)
        Note over Client,S3: Flow 3: Operator Reconciliation
        participant Operator as Operator Controller
        participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

        Operator->>K8sAPI: Watch LLMBatchGateway CRs<br/>TLS 1.2+, SA token
        K8sAPI-->>Operator: CR event notification
        Note over Operator: Render Helm charts in-memory<br/>(batch-gateway + async-processor)
        Operator->>K8sAPI: Server-side apply resources<br/>TLS 1.2+, SA token
        K8sAPI-->>Operator: Applied
        Operator->>K8sAPI: Delete orphaned resources<br/>TLS 1.2+, SA token
        Operator->>K8sAPI: Update CR status conditions<br/>TLS 1.2+, SA token
    end
